  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Stepping Up Universal Access: A Multi-Sectoral Partnership Response to TB/HIV at the Community Level - Lesotho (01-Jul-2016-30-Jun-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lesotho, TB/HIV, Pact, Inc. (Pact, Inc.)This program has the following goals: To eliminate mother to child transmission of HIV to below 2% by 2018.  To reduce new HIV infections and HIV related mortality by 50% by 2018.  To reduce TB prevalence by 25% and TB mortality by 50% relative to 2008 rates by 2018. The objectives of this program are: Eliminate mother to child transmission of HIV by 2017/18.  Enrol and retain 90% of eligible PLHIV on ART by 2020.  To achieve 70% TB case detection while increasing treatment success rate to 90% by 2018.  To address key Health System barriers which include governance and leadership at all levels, human resources for health (HRH), procurement and supply management (PSCM), and strategic information management.  To increase DST coverage to 95% of prioritized patients (re-treatment cases) and treat all identified MDR TB cases to achieve a treatment success rate of 75% by 2018..  To reduce mortality rate among TB/HIV co-infected patients to less than 5% by 2018</narrative>
  </description>
